Why M10_03: Gronow+21a (discussion of the shell masses) name only the thin-shell models M08_03, M09_03, M10_03 and M10_02 as candidates for
normal SNe Ia (observations disfavour 56Ni and Ti, Cr in the shell ejecta); of these M10_03 has the 1.0 Msun core
(56Ni 0.59 Msun, Table in gronow21a "select radioactive nuclides"). Gronow+21b: M10_03 fits the solar Ti, V, Cr ratios
at all metallicities; its [Mn/Fe] is below solar except at 3 Zsun. Sub-Chandrasekhar explosions are favoured by the Mn
and Ni abundances of dwarf galaxies (Kirby+19, ApJ 881, 45; de los Reyes+20, ApJ 891, 85). Per event at Z_sun:
[Ni/Fe] -0.04, [Mn/Fe] -0.09 (M10_05: -0.02, -0.03; the near-Chandrasekhar Seitenzahl+13 N100: +0.26, +0.18).
